# Phase 8 Walkthrough — Frontend Architecture & Real-Time Monaco IDE

## Overview of What Was Built
1. **React 19 + TypeScript + Vite Client Application**:
   - Running locally on `http://localhost:3000` with dev proxy forwarding `/api` to Express backend on port 4000.
   - Built a custom **Modern Obsidian Dark Design System** (`client/src/index.css`) with tokens, glassmorphism (`backdrop-filter: blur(16px)`), custom scrollbars, and glowing gradient accents (Emerald, Indigo, Cyan, Amber, Rose).
   - Modern typography: **Inter** (UI) and **JetBrains Mono** (Code & Telemetry).

2. **Split-Pane LeetCode-Equivalent Workspace (`src/pages/ProblemDetailPage.tsx`)**:
   - **Left Pane**: Problem description, constraints, interactive sample test cases with one-click copy buttons, and a Submissions history tab.
   - **Right Pane**: Multi-language selector (`PYTHON`, `CPP`, `JAVA`), VS-Code Monaco editor (`@monaco-editor/react`), starter templates, and evaluation control bar.

3. **Asynchronous Real-Time Polling Engine (`src/hooks/useSubmissionPolling.ts`)**:
   - Polling engine tracking `QUEUED` -> `RUNNING` -> Terminal verdict with timeout and memory leak protection.
   - Live telemetry verdict card (`src/components/VerdictCard.tsx`): Execution time (ms), memory (MB), per-testcase pass breakdown, and compiler error accordion.

4. **Authentication, Problem Catalog & Submissions Log**:
   - Persistent JWT auth context with one-click demo credentials (`user@codejudge.com` / `user123`, `admin@codejudge.com` / `admin123`).
   - Filterable problem list with real-time search, difficulty tabs, and pagination.
   - User submissions log with full telemetry breakdown.

